       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US), so this is about twice the limit.\n- A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy or your attending first."
      }
