       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin at 1,700 mg per dose and 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. The main risk is lactic acidosis, which can be severe and life-threatening.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range right away.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or whatever dose you choose up to that limit.\n- **Hold the order while you check with pharmacy or your attending.** If there's a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a transcription issue, they can sort it out. It would then be entered through their review.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it now."
